<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gharm</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Garm</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gharm is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rasht">Rasht</a> valley of central Tajikistan, on the Surkhob river, and the traditional name of the surrounding mountain region. In the 1920s it was a centre of Basmachi resistance to Soviet rule, and in later decades many of its people were resettled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> lands of the south. In the civil war of 1992–1997 the region was a stronghold of the Islamic opposition.</p></div>
